+# ISel / peephole ROI (2026-09-01)
+
+Godbolt-oracle distillation of high-ROI x86-64 codegen patterns from
+`engineering/kernels/isel_roi.c` vs GCC 16.2 / Clang 23.1 / ICC 2021.10 /
+ICX latest. Local A/B vs gcc 14.2 `-O2`. ANDN already fused — not
+re-implemented. Loop rotation stays opt-in; MachInst stays off on large
+loops.
+
+## Landed (this session)
+
+1. **Acc dest popcnt/lzcnt/tzcnt without staging movq.**
+   `emit_bitcount_direct` writes `popcntl %edi, %eax` instead of
+   `movq %rdi, %rax; popcntl %eax, %eax`.
+2. **Register-direct Clz/Ctz** (same two-operand form as Popcount).
+3. **Intel false-dependency xor** before popcnt/lzcnt/tzcnt when dest ≠ src
+   (`xorl %eax, %eax; popcntl %edi, %eax` — GCC's shape).
+4. **PF-16 `movl` on `operand_to_rax`** for non-negative imm32.
+5. **PF-16 `movl` on `operand_to_rcx`**.
+6. **`const_as_imm32_typed` in `emit_alu_reg_direct`** — Knuth hash
+   `imull $-1640531535, %edi, %edi` instead of `movabsq` + `imull %eax`.
+7. **MachInst S32 unsigned imm32** (`const_as_imm32_size` / `emit_alu_operand_r`).
+8. **MachInst `cmp $0` → `test`** (`lower_cmp` and `lower_cmp_branch`).
+9. **32-bit unsigned `cmov`** (`emit_cmov_typed`; signed I32 stays `cmovq`
+   because `cmovl` zero-extends dest).
+10. **`is_read_modify_write` dest-only** for popcnt/lzcnt/tzcnt/andn/blsr/blsi/bzhi.
+11. **`is_full_write` dest-only** for the same mnemonics (syntactic DCE fallback).
+12. **`is_32bit_zero_extend_write` += popcntl/lzcntl/tzcntl/andnl/blsrl/blsil/bzhil**
+    (kills identity `movl %eax, %eax` / `cltq` after bitcounts).
+13. **Skip identity `movl %eax, %eax`** in `operand_to_rax_i32`.
+14. **Acc-path `imull $imm` typed** (`try_emit_acc_immediate`).
+15. **`candidate_uses_32bit_dest` += popcntl/lzcntl/tzcntl/andnl**
+    (movq→movl copy narrowing after a 32-bit bitcount).
+
+## Measured (post-impl `/tmp/isel/{lccc,gcc}.s`, `-O3 -march=x86-64-v3`)
+
+| kernel | LCCC insns | GCC 14.2 insns | note |
+|---|---:|---:|---|
+| popcount32 | 3 | 3 | `popcntl %edi,%eax`; leftover `movq` gone; identity `movl %eax,%eax` remains vs GCC `xorl` |
+| popcount64 | 3 | 3 | `popcntq`; leftover `cltq` vs GCC `xorl` |
+| clz32 / ctz32 | 3 | 3 | dest-direct into `%edi` then `movl` to `%eax` |
+| andn32 | 2 | 2 | matches (`andnl`) |
+| hash_mul | 3 | 2 | signed-imm32 `imull`; extra `movl %edi,%eax` |
+| cmp0 | 6 | 4 | **`testl`** (was `cmpl $0`); extra `movslq` |
+| min_u32 | 4 | 4 | same count; still `cmovbq` (Select ty not U32 in IR) |
+| mul3/5/9 | 3 | 2 | `leaq` + `movl` vs GCC `leal …, %eax` |
+| zero / zext_load / lea_index | match | match | |
+| rotl32 | 16 | 4 | still open (`roll`) |
+| blsr32 / blsi32 / bzhi32 | 4/5/12 | 2/2/5 | no ISel pattern match |
+
+Godbolt CE (see `engineering/notes/2026-09-01-isel-roi-oracle.md` and
+`engineering/evidence/godbolt/isel_roi/`):
+
+- `andn32` / `min_u32`: LCCC ties best (2 / 4).
+- `popcount32` / `clz32`: LCCC 3, GCC 16.2 3, Clang/ICX 2.
+- `hash_mul` / `mul3` / `cmp0`: LCCC 3/3/6 vs best 2/2/4.
+- `rotl32`: 16 vs GCC/ICX 4 (largest remaining gap).
+- ICC on `popcount32` is 16 (no BMI, `__popcnt` SWAR) — ignore as oracle for BMI.
+
+## Correctness
+
+`engineering/kernels/isel_roi_driver.c` linked against the kernels:
+
+- LCCC `-O3 -march=x86-64-v3` vs gcc `-O2 -march=x86-64-v3`: **stdout MATCH**.
+
+Unit tests (fastbuild): `codegen::isel` 8/8; `peephole` 442 pass / 6 ignored;
+`dead_writes` leftover-movq-before-popcnt/lzcnt pass.
+
+gzip `longest_match` stack-mem: **not recompiled** (no `deflate.c` in this
+workspace). Diffs are ISel/peephole classifiers for dest-only BMI, typed
+imm32, `cmp $0`→`test`, unsigned 32-bit cmov — they do not grow frames.
+Do not enable MachInst on large loops; rotation stays opt-in (`env -u
+CCC_LOOP_ROTATE` for default-off A/B).
+
+## Still open (next session)
+
+- `rotl32` is 16 insns vs GCC `roll %cl, %eax` — variable rotate + ternary.
+- `blsr`/`blsi`/`bzhi` ISel (encoder exists, no IR pattern match).
+- MachInst `Lea` is always `leaq`; 32-bit `mul3` is `leaq`+`movl` vs GCC `leal …, %eax`.
+- Identity `movl %eax, %eax` after `popcntl` into eax (cast/copy, not leftover staging movq).
+- `min_u32` still `cmovbq` because Select IR type is not U32 (do not blindly
+  `cmovl` signed I32).
+- Do **not** retarget 64-bit `leaq` under 32-bit `movl`.
