+# Post-merge audit — PRs #325–#328 on `453cbea` (2026-09-01)
+
+HEAD = `origin/main` `453cbea`. Rotation stays **opt-in**. Fastbuild.
+
+## Merge
+
+`git diff 59d6f29 origin/main -- src/passes/loop_rotate.rs` is #325's
+pred-label comment only. Code already used `(pre_op, header_label)`.
+Guard D/E, univsr skip, unroll Copy-INIT, bepre `latest_dep` are on main
+via #327.
+
+| PR | What | Verdict |
+|---|---|---|
+| #325 | SCCP + use-def + IR verifier + pred-label | Sound. SCCP trusts phi preds; stale preheader label was the latent bug. Test `loop_rotate_stale_phi_pred`. |
+| #326 | RA-09 commutative ALU self-op | Sound. `op %rax, %dest` when lhs in acc and rhs homed in dest; Sub staged through rax. Test `ra09_selfop_xor` (-O3). |
+| #327 | PF-17 remaining-three | Sound. Guard D/E, univsr skip, unroll Copy-INIT. |
+| #328 | baseline popcount SWAR | Sound Hamming-weight sequence (same as Clang/ICC/ICX). |
+
+## 21-name A/B vs GCC 14.2 -O2
+
+**ROT-ON 22 MATCH / 0 FAIL** (original 15 + seq / while_dec / stale_phi_pred
++ ra09_selfop_xor + clz_ctz_popcount_target_isa). ROT-OFF also MATCH.
+`CCC_VERIFY_IR=abort` on `loop_rotate_stale_phi_pred` compiles.
+
+## Polish landed this audit
+
+- `CCC_LOOP_ROTATE` is truthy-only (`1`/`true`/`yes`/`on`). Empty / `0`
+  no longer silently enables (`is_err()` footgun). `CCC_NO_LOOP_ROTATE`
+  is implemented (was documented, never checked).
+- Guard C comment no longer claims `(pre_op, pre_label)`.
+- `loop_rotate_seq_loops.env` sets `CCC_DISABLE_PASSES=vectorize` so both
+  sequential loops actually rotate (Vec* bodies made the test a no-op).
+  Confirmed: SUCCESS header=1 and header=4, output `36` MATCH gcc.
+- `godbolt.py` `clang` → CE `cclang2310` (Clang 23.1.0). Aliases
+  `clang23` / `clang23.1` added.
+- univsr `reject_nonzero_init_counter` latch incoming is BlockId(2)
+  (unrotated), not the header.
+
+## Godbolt oracles (GCC 16.2, Clang 23.1, ICC 2021.10, ICX latest)
+
+Kernels: `engineering/kernels/popcount_swar.c`,
+`engineering/kernels/loop_rotate_sum.c`.
+
+### popcount32, `-O3 -march=x86-64` (baseline, no POPCNT)
+
+| compiler | insns | shape |
+|---|---|---|
+| LCCC | 20 | SWAR + push/pop %rcx + redundant `movl %eax,%eax` |
+| Clang 23.1 | 16 | same SWAR, no save/restore, reuses `%edi` |
+| ICC 2021.10 | 16 | same SWAR |
+| ICX latest | 16 | same SWAR |
+| GCC 16.2 | 5 | **libgcc call** `__popcountdi2` (not inlined) |
+
+LCCC's inline SWAR is the right baseline (no libgcc). Extra cost vs
+Clang is the conservative %rcx save (accumulator-mode may have staged
+a live value there — do **not** drop blindly) and a redundant zext.
+
+### popcount32, `-O3 -march=x86-64-v3` (hardware POPCNT)
+
+| compiler | insns | asm |
+|---|---|---|
+| Clang 23.1 / ICX | 2 | `popcntl %edi, %eax; ret` |
+| GCC 16.2 | 3 | `xorl %eax,%eax; popcntl %edi,%eax; ret` (false-dep break) |
+| LCCC | 4 | `movq %rdi,%rax; popcntl %edi,%eax; movl %eax,%eax; ret` |
+| ICC 2021.10 | 16 | still SWAR (`-march=x86-64-v3` not honoured on CE's icc) |
+
+Dead `movq %rdi,%rax` before `popcntl %edi,%eax` is leftover staging.
+Follow-up, not a miscompile.
+
+### sum_arr, `-O2`, LCCC with `CCC_LOOP_ROTATE=1` + vectorize off
+
+Rotated form is present (test-at-bottom `cmpl; jge exit`). Phi-elim
+still splits the self-loop into body + copy trampoline + `jmp` (the
+known TASK item: re-land the narrower self-loop copy-placement gate).
+GCC 16.2: 12-insn pointer-IV do-while. Clang 23.1 vectorizes at -O2
+(39 insns). Correctness MATCH vs local GCC; do not flip default-ON.
+
+## Do not
+
+- Do not flip `CCC_LOOP_ROTATE` default until the 474 corpus is green.
+- Do not re-try tight Guard E (copy-prop hides the outer phi dest).
+- Do not drop univsr skip of rotated self-loop pointer IVs.
+- Do not drop the %rcx/%rdx push around baseline SWAR without a liveness
+  proof — accumulator-mode can have those registers live.
+- ZSTD P0 still needs kernel tree + qemu (absent here).
